{"duration": 49.999, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A soldier punches twelve tiny dots into paper in the dead of night.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.508}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His comrades laugh, saying the code is useless and too slow.", "start": 3.928, "end": 7.097}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Blind teen Louis Braille watches the demo at his school.", "start": 7.517, "end": 10.234}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He grabs the same slate and stylus.", "start": 10.454, "end": 12.35}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He spends months feeling each pattern.", "start": 12.57, "end": 14.353}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Then he halves the grid to three high and two wide.", "start": 14.573, "end": 17.034}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like turning a bulky novel into a pocket\u2011size cheat sheet you can feel with one fingertip.", "start": 17.454, "end": 22.809}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Barbier\u2019s army night\u2011writing used twelve raised points to spell sounds, but soldiers could not master it.", "start": 23.229, "end": 29.003}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Braille cut the pattern in half, using only six dots to stand for letters, numbers and punctuation.", "start": 29.223, "end": 34.781}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Six dots sit comfortably under a single finger.", "start": 35.001, "end": 37.341}, {"beat": 4, "text": "A reader can feel a whole character in one quick touch.", "start": 37.561, "end": 40.232}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Writers can punch the dots faster than they could trace letters.", "start": 40.452, "end": 43.44}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the system meant for soldiers became the world\u2019s universal language for the blind.", "start": 43.86, "end": 48.879}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.145, "end": 0.195, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "soldier", "start": 0.27, "end": 0.695, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "punches", "start": 0.745, "end": 1.095, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "twelve", "start": 1.17, "end": 1.445, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "tiny", "start": 1.52, 